WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:04.830
There's been speculation about another Jackass
sequel since the credits rolled on Jackass

00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:06.569
3D in 2010.

00:00:06.569 --> 00:00:11.030
That last incarnation of the grossout prankfest
was so popular that Paramount released Jackass

00:00:11.030 --> 00:00:14.769
3.5 a year later, which was full of unrated
and outtakes from 3D.

00:00:14.769 --> 00:00:22.070
"This is the flying d--- high five!"

00:00:22.070 --> 00:00:25.840
But fans still haven't had their fill of the
death-defying stunts and excrement-centered

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:28.480
pranks they've grown to love in the first
three movies.

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:32.930
In the six years since Jackass 3.5, there's
been a ton of buzz about the next installment.

00:00:32.930 --> 00:00:37.080
Paramount Pictures supposedly registered a
bunch of Jackass 4-related domain names.

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:41.721
Johnny Knoxville said in a Reddit AMA that
there were "no plans for another movie," but

00:00:41.721 --> 00:00:43.440
they were "open to doing another."

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:47.460
Director Jeff Tremaine announced it would
be shot in Australia, and Bam Margera even

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:51.660
let it slip that they were toying with a Jackass
sequel named in honor of the crew's late buddy,

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:52.660
Ryan Dunn.

00:00:52.660 --> 00:00:54.400
"We just started talking about it.

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:58.120
We want to call it 'We're Not Dunn Yet', like
D-U-N-N."

00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:02.030
So why hasn't another sequel happened yet?

00:01:02.030 --> 00:01:05.719
Is there a worldwide shortage of tasers and
poo-cannons that we're unaware of?

00:01:05.719 --> 00:01:06.719
Not quite.

00:01:06.719 --> 00:01:09.530
Here's why we never got to see Jackass 4.

00:01:09.530 --> 00:01:10.640
Johnny Hollywood

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:14.200
Though the show and movies were definitely
a collaborative effort, Johnny Knoxville has

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:16.979
always been the pointman for the wild Jackass
crew.

00:01:16.979 --> 00:01:20.700
As the de facto host of the show, Knoxville
brought a certain star quality that helped

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:25.000
transform what were essentially underground
skate videos into a multi-million dollar TV

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:26.359
and film concept.

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:29.320
"Hi, I'm Johnny Knoxville and welcome to Jackass!"

00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:35.829
Between the first two Jackass movies, Knoxville
made the jump to actual films, with starring

00:01:35.829 --> 00:01:38.210
roles in The Ringer and The Dukes of Hazzard
reboot.

00:01:38.210 --> 00:01:42.430
And yes, he still returned for Jackass 3D,
but he's also talked about the desire to make

00:01:42.430 --> 00:01:44.490
films with a narrative.

00:01:44.490 --> 00:01:48.639
In 2017, Knoxville completed such a film,
which he described to Complex as "not Jackass

00:01:48.639 --> 00:01:52.299
but all the stunts are done in the vein of,"
adding, "It's a scripted film with me doing

00:01:52.299 --> 00:01:53.719
the stunts."

00:01:53.719 --> 00:01:58.330
That film is Action Park, and it's based on
a real New Jersey theme park that had a notorious

00:01:58.330 --> 00:02:02.659
reputation for its lax safety policy that
resulted in many cases of guest injuries,

00:02:02.659 --> 00:02:04.009
and even six deaths.

00:02:04.009 --> 00:02:07.799
During an interview on Jimmy Kimmel Live,
Knoxville listed the litany of injuries he

00:02:07.799 --> 00:02:09.720
suffered while shooting Action Park:

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:15.840
"Two concussions, a broken hand, a sprained
knee, a torn MCL, and I got stitches on this

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:16.840
side."

00:02:16.960 --> 00:02:17.980
But that wasn't even worst of it:

00:02:18.220 --> 00:02:21.320
"I get home from the emergency room from my
second concussion.

00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:26.570
And I blow my nose, and when I blow my nose,
my left eye pops out of its socket."

00:02:26.570 --> 00:02:31.240
So, while Knoxville clearly still has the
itch to perform crazy stunt work, it also

00:02:31.240 --> 00:02:34.080
seems like he wants to tell a story, too.

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:35.080
Star schedules

00:02:35.080 --> 00:02:38.640
With Knoxville's career more or less taking
off, the rest of the guys have had to turn

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:41.020
to other venues to keep the paychecks coming
in.

00:02:41.020 --> 00:02:45.940
Steve-O is busy nurturing a fledgling stand-up
comedy act, while Chris Pontius, Wee Man,

00:02:45.940 --> 00:02:50.010
Preston Lacy, and Dave England have basically
taken the Jackass concept and applied it to

00:02:50.010 --> 00:02:51.010
a live show.

00:02:51.010 --> 00:02:55.870
In 2016, they went to Australia with their
"Filthy Seppo Tour," an on-stage mix of stunts

00:02:55.870 --> 00:02:57.310
and comedy routines.

00:02:57.310 --> 00:03:01.110
But for the most part, they seem to be just
biding their time until the next Jackass reunion

00:03:01.110 --> 00:03:02.750
brings them all back together.

00:03:02.750 --> 00:03:06.750
In an interview with The Daily Journal, Preston
Lacy admitted that the next Jackass sequel

00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:08.870
hinges entirely on Knoxville's involvement.

00:03:08.870 --> 00:03:10.190
"Hopefully, we'll do another movie.

00:03:10.190 --> 00:03:12.470
We're just waiting on Johnny Knoxville's schedule.

00:03:12.470 --> 00:03:15.560
… In Hollywood, unless you have a contract,
nothing is nothing."

00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:18.660
Steve-O seems to have the same sentiments,
but he put it a lot more bluntly.

00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:19.660
He told UPROXX:

00:03:19.660 --> 00:03:22.940
"...some of the guys are sort of less busy
than other guys, and kind of feeling really

00:03:22.940 --> 00:03:25.080
desperate to get another movie going.

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:28.540
Every once in a while an e-mail will be sent
to everybody from one of the guys in the cast

00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:29.540
saying, “Come on!

00:03:29.540 --> 00:03:30.540
Come on!

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:31.540
Let’s make a movie.

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:32.540
Let’s make a movie.”

00:03:32.540 --> 00:03:35.020
It seems like a pretty clear sign that without
Johnny Knoxville's involvement, that movie

00:03:35.020 --> 00:03:37.490
will probably never get off the ground.

00:03:37.490 --> 00:03:39.200
A dark cloud

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:43.440
Ryan Dunn's tragic loss in a drunk-driving
accident came right on the heels of the release

00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:48.040
of Jackass 3.5 and had a devastating effect
on the Jackass crew.

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:51.931
Dunn and his passenger, Zachary Hartwell,
fatally crashed when Dunn lost control of

00:03:51.931 --> 00:03:57.250
his Porsche which he was reportedly driving
"between 132 and 140" mph.

00:03:57.250 --> 00:04:01.110
His blood alcohol content was .196 at the
time of the crash.

00:04:01.110 --> 00:04:05.370
Both director Jeff Tremaine and Johnny Knoxville
penned touching tributes to their fallen friend

00:04:05.370 --> 00:04:06.730
on Knoxville's blog.

00:04:06.730 --> 00:04:10.510
In Tremaine's entry, he writes, "He was such
a huge part of our family and it is forever

00:04:10.510 --> 00:04:11.990
changed without him."

00:04:11.990 --> 00:04:15.910
Dunn was also Bam Margera's best friend, and
Margera later admitted that he'd spiraled

00:04:15.910 --> 00:04:17.669
out of control after Dunn's death.

00:04:17.669 --> 00:04:22.000
During an episode of Family Therapy, Margera
said, "Since Dunn got in that crash, everything

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:25.860
changed dramatically, and instead of drinking
for fun with your friends, [it] turned into

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:27.159
drinking to forget."

00:04:27.159 --> 00:04:31.389
While a sequel is still possible, the loss
of a beloved friend and castmate certainly

00:04:31.389 --> 00:04:35.229
cast a dark cloud over any future Jackass
project.

00:04:35.229 --> 00:04:36.990
Margera's sobriety

00:04:36.990 --> 00:04:40.689
After Dunn's fatal accident, Bam Margera's
drinking spiralled out of control, leading

00:04:40.689 --> 00:04:44.759
Steve-O to express his doubts over whether
Margera could even get himself together for

00:04:44.759 --> 00:04:45.759
a sequel.

00:04:45.759 --> 00:04:50.590
In a 2016 Reddit AMA, he said, "If Bam can
stay sober and healthy, I suppose it's possible,

00:04:50.590 --> 00:04:51.659
but I think it's unlikely."

00:04:51.659 --> 00:04:56.370
Meanwhile, it seems like Margera is ready
to throw himself back into some kind chaotic,

00:04:56.370 --> 00:04:57.379
prank-filled atmosphere.

00:04:57.379 --> 00:05:01.820
In an interview for the Gorilla Flicks blog,
Margera opened up about getting healthy, refocusing

00:05:01.820 --> 00:05:06.150
on skating during a lengthy European hiatus,
and possibly getting another installment of

00:05:06.150 --> 00:05:07.360
Jackass going.

00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:11.580
He's even got a concept ready to go, which
he's tentatively calling Jackass Hotel, which

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:15.330
would trick the entire cast into thinking
they're checking into a hotel to start shooting

00:05:15.330 --> 00:05:18.610
the movie, only the hotel is already rigged
with cameras and pranks.

00:05:18.610 --> 00:05:19.879
He explained the concept, saying:

00:05:19.879 --> 00:05:22.900
"Before they know it we just film the movie
without anyone’s knowledge.

00:05:22.900 --> 00:05:24.210
We f--- with everybody.

00:05:24.210 --> 00:05:27.169
Every room is rigged, everybody’s there
to prank everybody.

00:05:27.169 --> 00:05:28.590
Prank after prank after prank."

00:05:28.590 --> 00:05:31.889
But aside from the fact that he basically
ruined the possibility of that concept by

00:05:31.889 --> 00:05:36.289
talking about it, Margera doesn't even seem
that committed to the Jackass brand anymore.

00:05:36.289 --> 00:05:37.539
He closed the interview, saying:

00:05:37.539 --> 00:05:38.539
"Dear Tremaine…

00:05:38.539 --> 00:05:42.009
Let’s figure out something to film again,
whether it’s a jackass or a something else.

00:05:42.009 --> 00:05:46.159
I like this new Viceland channel and I have
a couple ideas, so I’m ready to film again.

00:05:46.159 --> 00:05:49.250
I’ve spent a lot of time sitting at bars
and drinking, but I’m over that now.

00:05:49.250 --> 00:05:51.060
I’ve had enough."

00:05:51.060 --> 00:05:52.490
Steve-O isn't interested

00:05:52.490 --> 00:05:56.409
For his part, Steve-O seems like he's just
plain moved on from the show and movies that

00:05:56.409 --> 00:05:57.409
made him famous.

00:05:57.409 --> 00:06:00.460
The star famously battled with his own addiction
issues during the show.

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:09.249
"Umm, using ketamine, PCP, cocaine, nitrous
oxide…"

00:06:09.249 --> 00:06:12.569
But he's since cleaned up, and he told The
Daily Beast that on top of focusing on his

00:06:12.569 --> 00:06:16.189
new stand-up career, he's also searching for
a new purpose in his life.

00:06:16.189 --> 00:06:19.319
"Now my goal is to find separation between
me and that character.

00:06:19.319 --> 00:06:23.509
To find separation between Steve-O and whoever
I am—and more than that, for whoever I am

00:06:23.509 --> 00:06:25.990
to find fulfillment and validation from within."

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:29.740
That's a big turnaround for a guy who once
dove head-first into Mike Tyson's fist, just

00:06:29.740 --> 00:06:30.620
because he could.

00:06:35.680 --> 00:06:39.520
But fans don't have to worry too much about
the possibility of a Steve-O-less Jackass

00:06:39.529 --> 00:06:40.809
4 since he also told Vice:

00:06:40.809 --> 00:06:44.250
"I almost don't want there to be another Jackass
movie because I've worked hard to build my

00:06:44.250 --> 00:06:48.090
own momentum, and for me to have a little
bit of traction, and to be able to be getting

00:06:48.090 --> 00:06:50.240
away with having a career beyond Jackass…

00:06:50.240 --> 00:06:51.669
I want to keep that going.

00:06:51.669 --> 00:06:54.559
But I would never turn down anything Jackass-related."

00:06:54.559 --> 00:06:55.559
Aging out

00:06:55.559 --> 00:06:58.789
Hard to believe, but Johnny Knoxville is now
closer to 50 than 40.

00:06:58.789 --> 00:07:02.849
And in the two decades that Knoxville battered
his body for the show and movies, he's racked

00:07:02.849 --> 00:07:07.800
up innumerable injuries, once after getting
viciously head-punched by Butterbean, and

00:07:07.800 --> 00:07:09.550
once after flipping a golf cart.

00:07:09.550 --> 00:07:12.740
Steve-O brought up the cold hard truth about
aging in an email to his buddies:

00:07:12.740 --> 00:07:14.360
"Hey, I love working with you guys.

00:07:14.360 --> 00:07:15.689
We're all great friends.

00:07:15.689 --> 00:07:19.370
It's something really special that we have,
but with that said, as excited as I am to

00:07:19.370 --> 00:07:23.150
work with you guys, if we're going to another
project we need to figure out a way to get

00:07:23.150 --> 00:07:25.309
out in front of it and acknowledge we're old.

00:07:25.309 --> 00:07:26.309
Because we're old."

00:07:26.309 --> 00:07:29.710
And even though he's not exactly thrilled
with the prospect of aging, he also told The

00:07:29.710 --> 00:07:33.839
Daily Beast, "Now I'm in my forties and I
can't post a picture without someone commenting,

00:07:33.839 --> 00:07:36.710
'Dude, you got old'...I think I'm pretty realistic
about it.

00:07:36.710 --> 00:07:40.659
It just points to what's important is to find
separation from that."

00:07:40.659 --> 00:07:42.099
Director projects

00:07:42.099 --> 00:07:45.289
Jeff Tremaine is the director and driving
force behind Jackass.

00:07:45.289 --> 00:07:49.199
His skate magazine, Big Brother, served as
the inspiration for the show, and even employed

00:07:49.199 --> 00:07:51.800
almost the entire cast before they ever had
a deal with MTV.

00:07:51.800 --> 00:07:55.370
"I thought I could make a TV show out of it,
and MTV just loved it.

00:07:55.370 --> 00:07:56.599
They just ordered a series."

00:07:56.599 --> 00:08:00.710
And because hanging out with notorious bad
boys is kind of Tremaine's thing, he parlayed

00:08:00.710 --> 00:08:04.759
his Jackass success to tell the story of "the
world's most notorious rock band," Mötley

00:08:04.759 --> 00:08:05.759
Crüe.

00:08:05.759 --> 00:08:09.659
In 2016, he produced a documentary about the
band's final tour, and recently announced

00:08:09.659 --> 00:08:13.499
that he was finally been attached to direct
a feature biopic about the band, called The

00:08:13.499 --> 00:08:14.499
Dirt.

00:08:14.499 --> 00:08:17.559
Tremaine told ScreenCrush, "Dirt is something
I pursued with everything I had.

00:08:17.559 --> 00:08:21.430
I've wanted to make this going back to 2001,
when we were just planning the first Jackass

00:08:21.430 --> 00:08:22.430
movie."

00:08:22.430 --> 00:08:25.969
Outside of the Jackass-sphere, Tremaine has
been chained to the skater/prank show genre,

00:08:25.969 --> 00:08:30.960
with producer credits for Nitro Circus, Dudesons
in America, Rob Dyrdek's Fantasy Factory,

00:08:30.960 --> 00:08:31.960
and Ridiculousness.

00:08:31.960 --> 00:08:35.240
But it seems he's ready to take a legitimate
seat in the director's chair.

00:08:35.240 --> 00:08:39.459
Plus, as far as we can tell, a 2014 Daily
Mail interview was the last time Tremaine

00:08:39.459 --> 00:08:42.279
even spoke to the press about another Jackass
installment.

00:08:42.279 --> 00:08:46.240
Sounds like he's in no rush to get back to
it, and without Tremaine behind the camera,

00:08:46.240 --> 00:08:48.350
Jackass 4 will probably never happen.

00:08:48.350 --> 00:08:52.080
"Hello, my name's Johnny Knoxville and I'm
about to end this movie."

00:08:53.540 --> 00:08:55.220
Thanks for watching!

00:08:55.560 --> 00:08:56.560
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:08:56.740 --> 00:08:58.900
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

